%% How GSDiagram is tested: the three suites, what each runs against, and what npm run release does with them.
flowchart TD
    release([npm run release]) --> unit
    unit --> ext
    ext --> ui
    ui --> package[vsce package: gsdiagram-version.vsix]

    subgraph unitSuite [Unit: npm test]
        unit[43 tests in dev/testing/unit] --> shared[GSDiagram/shared: processes, folder, check, layout, architecture, model, review, generate]
    end

    subgraph extSuite [Extension: npm run test:vscode]
        ext[3 tests in dev/testing/vscode] --> testVsCode[VS Code test instance on dev/testing/fixture]
    end

    subgraph uiSuite [UI: npm run test:ui, its own Node project in dev/testing/playwright]
        ui[65 tests in dev/testing/playwright/tests] --> fresh[A fresh copy of dev/testing/fixture per test]
        fresh --> start[VS Code 1.144.0 from .vscode-test, clean environment, under xvfb]
        start --> drive[Playwright drives it: command palette, Problems panel, lenses, editors, the diagram page]
        drive -->|passed| next[Next test]
        drive -->|failed| evidence[Screenshot, trace, and error context in test-results/output]
    end

    ui --> specs[analyse 4, check 12, editor 22, generate 6, processes 8, settings 7, sidebar 6]
